From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:11:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 04/11] wifi: b43: encrypt protected management
 frames in software

With management frame protection, unicast robust management frames
(action frames such as SA Query and Radio Measurement, deauthentication,
disassociation) are CCMP-protected. For those, the CCM nonce has the
Management flag set and the AAD keeps the frame's subtype bits (IEEE
Std 802.11-2020, 12.5.3.3.3 and 12.5.3.3.4; ccmp_special_blocks() in
mac80211). When the key is in hardware, b43's crypto engine encrypts
them as if they were QoS data frames instead: decrypting frames
captured from a BCM4331 shows a nonce without the Management flag, and
an AAD with the subtype bits masked and a zero QoS Control field
appended (the subtypes of Action and Deauthentication frames have the
bit that marks a QoS data frame). The peer can't decrypt them.

Against an AP with PMF, the AP got no usable response to its SA Query
and Radio Measurement requests, and after a disconnect and reconnect it
started an SA Query procedure, apparently having missed our protected
Deauthentication. With this change all of them decrypt correctly.

Set IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_SW_MGMT_TX on CCMP keys so that mac80211
encrypts management frames itself; data frames still use the hardware.
carl9170, ath5k, rtlwifi and mt76x02 do the same for crypto engines
that can't handle it, see e.g. commit 23405236460b ("mt76: fix
transmission of encrypted management frames").

Fixes: 75d057bda1fb ("b43: Fix connection problem with WPA3")
Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
index 13f6d9623c8a..3eabe7b41add 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -4267,6 +4267,11 @@ static int b43_op_set_key(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, enum set_key_cmd cmd,
 		key->flags |= IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_IV;
 		if (algorithm == B43_SEC_ALGO_TKIP)
 			key->flags |= IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_MMIC;
+		/* The engine gets CCMP of protected management frames
+		 * wrong; let mac80211 encrypt those.
+		 */
+		if (algorithm == B43_SEC_ALGO_AES)
+			key->flags |= IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_SW_MGMT_TX;
 		break;
 	case DISABLE_KEY: {
 		err = b43_key_clear(dev, key->hw_key_idx);
